      "problem": "Given $h(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+6}}{\\sqrt{2x-1}},$ find $h(5).$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $5$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(5) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2(5)+6}}{\\sqrt{2(5)-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{10+6}}{\\sqrt{10-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
